# Session documents — the working notes a Claude Code session writes and reads.
# They are how a session hands off to the next one, not part of the app, and
# they date fast; the contracts they describe live in the tracked README and in
# GradeBridge2026/CLAUDE.md. Keep them local.
#
# This block existed, with this reasoning, while nineteen process documents were
# tracked anyway — nine of them REPORT_* under tests/captures/, which the list
# did not name. So: no leading slash on any pattern, because these arrive in
# subdirectories as often as at the root, and `tests/no-process-records.mjs`
# fails the suite if one is ever tracked. An ignore file is not a guard; it does
# nothing about a file somebody adds with `-f`, and that is how these got in.
HANDOFF_*.md
COMPLETION_*.md
WORKORDER_*.md
WORK_ORDERS_*.md
CORRECTION_*.md
REPORT_*.md
DIRECTIVE_*.md
DECISION_*.md
SESSION_*.md
MILESTONE_*.md
NOTE_*.md
PLAN_*.md
SCHEDULE_*.md
RESUME_*.md
HANDOVER_*.md
BRIEF_*.md
START_HERE*.md
*_Memo_*.md
*_Test_Battery_*.md

# Generated capture set for the registration suite (npm run captures rebuilds it).
# Real photographs in tests/captures/real/ ARE tracked — they are the evidence.
tests/captures/synthetic/

# Photographs of other people's work. This repository is public and these images
# are not ours to publish: the `students/` captures are real submitted coursework
# and the `android/` set was contributed by a colleague for testing. They are the
# best evidence the capture pipeline has — LABELS.csv specifies all 41 rows —
# so the suite names the ones it cannot see rather than counting an absent
# photograph as agreement.
#
# The photographs that ARE tracked, in real/ and stale/, are the maintainer's
# own blank template with his own handwriting on it. See tests/captures/README.md.
tests/captures/students/
tests/captures/android/
# ...and anything a probe renders FROM them.
tests/captures/_probe/ios2_*
tests/captures/_probe/ios1_*
tests/captures/_probe/android*
